<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
  <title>Cyris Onboarding</title>
  <meta name="description" content="The guided setup of a new Cyris deployment: language, publish hours, sources, votes, notifications and the first issue.">
  <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&display=swap">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/style.css">
  <style>
    /* This page's own layout: one step at a time, over the step list that says
       where the reader is (ui-language.md §6 onboarding). Every control and
       role comes from style.css; a rule here that another page also needs
       belongs there. */
    body { font-size: calc(14px * var(--type-scale)); line-height: 1.6; min-height: 100vh; }
    a { color: inherit; }
    button, input, select, textarea { font: inherit; color: inherit; }
    .page { max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s-12) var(--s-4) var(--s-20); }
    .steps { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-2) var(--s-4); margin: 0 0 var(--s-8); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .steps li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-2); }
    .steps li::before { content: ""; width: 6px; height: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 50%; }
    .steps li.done::before { background: var(--text-dim); border-color: var(--text-dim); }
    .steps li[aria-current="step"] { color: var(--accent); }
    .steps li[aria-current="step"]::before { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
    .step { display: grid; gap: var(--s-6); }
    .step-head { display: grid; gap: var(--s-2); }
    .step-nav { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--s-8); }
    .vote-card { gap: var(--s-2); }
    .vote-card .title { font-weight: 600; font-size: calc(18px * var(--type-scale)); line-height: 1.3; text-decoration: none; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .vote-card .title:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .vote-card .seg { justify-self: start; margin-top: var(--s-1); }
    .add-feed { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-2); }
    .add-feed .input { flex: 1 1 14em; width: auto; min-width: 0; }
    #o-own .sources-check { margin-top: var(--s-4); }
    /* The opening takes what the site bar and the page's gutters leave of the
       viewport, so it never scrolls, and the stage takes what the sentence and
       the buttons leave of that. The sentence holds its place while it is
       hidden, so the stage does not jump when it shows. */
    .opening { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-5); height: calc(100svh - var(--bar-h) - var(--s-12) - var(--s-20)); }
    .opening-stage { position: relative; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
    .opening-stage canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
    /* A line of no height at the vanishing point, which the script sets: the
       logo centres on it without a transform, which §4 keeps for motion. */
    .opening-vp { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
    .opening-logo { padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-3); background: var(--bg); opacity: 0; }
    /* The site bar drops the name below 720px; the logo on the stage keeps it. */
    .opening-logo .brand-name { display: inline; }
    .opening-claim { text-wrap: balance; }
    .opening-claim[data-held] { visibility: hidden; }
    .opening-nav { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
{% with current="onboarding" %}{% include "_site_bar.html.j2" %}{% endwith %}
  <main class="page">
    {# The opening is not a step: no hash names it, so a reload on a step keeps
       that step. Its headlines are the server's sample pool
       (GET /api/onboarding/headlines), and the script runs its three beats. #}
    <section class="opening" id="o-opening" hidden>
      <div class="opening-stage" id="o-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <canvas id="o-canvas"></canvas>
        <div class="opening-vp"><span class="brand opening-logo" id="o-logo"><span class="brand-mark"></span><span class="brand-name">CYRIS</span></span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="heading opening-claim" id="o-claim" data-held>Too much, too fast. I’ll hold it for you; <em>you</em> say what matters.</p>
      <div class="opening-nav">
        <button class="btn secondary" type="button" id="o-skip-intro">Skip intro</button>
        <button class="btn primary" type="button" id="o-show" hidden>Show me how</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="label" id="o-progress">Step 1 of 6</span>
      <h1 class="display">Set up <em>cyris</em></h1>
      <p class="small">Six steps to your first issue. Skip any of them: a skipped step keeps its current value, and everything here can be changed later in Settings.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps" id="o-steps">
      <li class="label" data-step="language">Language</li>
      <li class="label" data-step="schedule">Publish hours</li>
      <li class="label" data-step="sources">Sources</li>
      <li class="label" data-step="votes">Votes</li>
      <li class="label" data-step="notify">Notifications</li>
      <li class="label" data-step="first-issue">First issue</li>
    </ol>

    <section class="step" data-step="language" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">Language and timezone</h2>
        <p class="small">The language each issue is written in, and the clock its publish hours are read in.</p>
        <p class="small" data-loading>Loading settings…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-output-language">Output language</label>
        <select class="select" id="o-output-language"></select>
        <p class="small">The language headlines and summaries are written in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-timezone">Timezone</label>
        <select class="select" id="o-timezone"></select>
        <p class="small">The clock the publish hours are read in.</p>
        <p class="small" id="o-timezone-detected" hidden>Detected from this browser, and not saved yet: Next saves it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="step" data-step="schedule" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">Publish hours</h2>
        <p class="small">When each day's two issues are published.</p>
        <p class="small" data-loading>Loading settings…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-morning">Morning</label>
        <input class="input" id="o-morning" type="number" min="0" max="23" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-evening">Evening</label>
        <input class="input" id="o-evening" type="number" min="0" max="23" autocomplete="off">
        <p class="small">Whole hours from 0 to 23, in the timezone of the step before; half hours are refused.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# The list is the server's (GET /api/onboarding/feeds), offered only while the
       sources table is empty, in two screens of this one step: its topics, then
       the chosen topics' feeds, one checklist per topic. The hash names the
       screen: #sources, then #sources/feeds. Each pick is posted to
       POST /api/sources as listed, less the list's own topics. #}
    <section class="step" data-step="sources" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">Sources</h2>
        <p class="small" data-screen="topics">The feeds this deployment reads, each a publisher's own feed. Pick the topics you follow; Next shows their feeds.</p>
        <p class="small" data-screen="feeds" hidden>The feeds of the topics you picked. Check the ones you read; Back changes the topics.</p>
        <p class="small" id="o-feeds-loading">Loading feeds…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field" data-screen="topics" id="o-topics-screen" hidden>
        <span class="label" id="o-topics-label">Topics</span>
        <div class="tiles" id="o-topics" role="group" aria-labelledby="o-topics-label"></div>
        <p class="small" id="o-feeds-hint">Pick topics to see their feeds. Next with none picked goes straight to adding your own feed.</p>
      </div>
      <div data-screen="feeds" id="o-feeds-screen" hidden>
        <div id="o-feeds"></div>
        {# A feed the list lacks, by its address or its site's home page: the
           server checks it (POST /api/onboarding/feed-check) and names it by its
           own title, and Next posts it with the picks, under Your feeds. #}
        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="o-own-url">Add your own feed</label>
          <div class="add-feed">
            <input class="input" id="o-own-url" type="url" inputmode="url" placeholder="https://example.com/feed.xml" autocomplete="off">
            <button class="btn secondary" type="button" id="o-own-add">Add</button>
          </div>
          <p class="small">A feed's address, or a site's home page that links one. It is named by the feed's own title.</p>
          <div class="notice" id="o-own-result" role="status" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <div id="o-own"></div>
        {# Fixed above the buttons: how many feeds Next sends, and past SLOW_PICKS
           in onboarding.js, that the Votes step waits for each of them. #}
        <p class="small" id="o-picked" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <p class="small" id="o-feeds-had" hidden>This deployment already has sources. Add more later under Sources in Settings; Next moves on.</p>
    </section>

    {# The cards are the server's (POST /api/onboarding/cards), read through the
       run's own RSS fetch; Next sends only the marked ones to POST /api/onboarding/votes. #}
    <section class="step" data-step="votes" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">Votes</h2>
        <p class="small">A few older articles from your feeds: mark the ones you would read and the ones you would not, and leave the rest. Next records each mark as a vote, so the first issue leaves those articles out.</p>
        <p class="small" id="o-cards-loading" aria-busy="true" hidden>Fetching the latest articles from your feeds. This can take a minute or two…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="notice err" id="o-cards-empty" hidden></div>
      <p class="small" id="o-cards-none" hidden></p>
      <div class="panel" id="o-cards" hidden></div>
    </section>

    <section class="step" data-step="notify" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">Notifications</h2>
        <p class="small">Where a finished issue is announced. Leave both empty to be notified nowhere.</p>
        <p class="small" data-loading>Loading settings…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-discord-webhook">Discord webhook</label>
        <input class="input" id="o-discord-webhook" type="text" placeholder="https://discord.com/api/webhooks/..." autocomplete="off">
        <p class="small">Paste the whole URL; it is saved once Discord confirms it exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-email-to">Email to</label>
        <input class="input" id="o-email-to" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="off">
        <p class="small">Leave it empty to send no mail. It must be a verified destination in Cloudflare Email Routing, and is saved once a test message reaches it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="o-email-from">Email from</label>
        <input class="input" id="o-email-from" type="email" placeholder="digest@your-domain" autocomplete="off">
        <p class="small">An address on your Email Routing domain.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# The run is the app Worker's own POST /run?period=&date=, the route any manual
       run takes. GET /api/onboarding/first-issue picks the key a later tick today
       cannot replace, and reads the run's outcome back from digest_runs. #}
    <section class="step" data-step="first-issue" hidden>
      <div class="step-head">
        <h2 class="heading">First issue</h2>
        <p class="small">Build an issue now from your feeds and votes, instead of waiting for the next publish hour. It runs as a scheduled issue does, notifications included, and Skip leaves the first issue to that hour.</p>
        <p class="small" id="o-issue-loading" aria-busy="true">Checking which issue comes first…</p>
      </div>
      <p class="small" id="o-issue-plan" hidden></p>
      <p class="small" id="o-vote-similarity" hidden></p>
    </section>

    <div class="step-nav">
      <button class="btn secondary" type="button" id="o-back">Back</button>
      <button class="btn secondary" type="button" id="o-skip">Skip</button>
      <button class="btn primary" type="button" id="o-next">Next</button>
      {# The last step's own action: it starts the run, and once a run fails it tries again. #}
      <button class="btn primary" type="button" id="o-start" hidden>Start the first issue</button>
      {# The way out, on the last step alone, once there is no run to start or one
         has been started. The mark is what keeps /settings from sending a
         deployment whose sources table is still empty straight back here. #}
      <a class="btn primary" id="o-finish" href="/settings?from=onboarding" hidden>Finish</a>
      <div class="notice" id="o-result" role="status" hidden></div>
    </div>
  </main>
<script src="/static/onboarding.js"></script>
{% include "_probe_script.html.j2" %}
</body>
</html>
